course: dictionary
lesson: 11351
title: Words with a sting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A zinger is a quick, clever, funny remark, often a sharp joke aimed at someone. Context clues help you find this. «A zinger is a sharp, funny line planned to make the other person look silly.» The words sharp, funny and look silly tell you it is a joke, not a sting.
explain: The word is informal, so you hear it in chatty talk, comedy and stories more than in school books. Zinger can also mean something surprising or striking, like a zinger of a question. Read the rest of the sentence to see which meaning fits.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «She delivered a zinger» should still make sense if you read it as «she made a quick, clever, funny remark». If it does, you have the right meaning.
fact: Zinger is an informal noun, so you will mostly hear it in everyday talk, comedy and stories.
fact: «Zinger» means a quick, clever and funny remark, often a sharp joke at someone.
fact: «Zinger» can also mean something surprising or striking, like a zinger of a question.
fact: Common phrases are deliver a zinger and a real zinger.
fact: Context clues such as sharp, funny and make the other person look silly show you what a zinger is.
exercise: «She delivered a zinger that made the whole class laugh.» What is a zinger here? | *A quick, clever, funny remark | A long, boring speech | A loud noise from the bell
exercise: «That was a zinger of a question.» What does zinger suggest here? | Something dull and slow | *Something surprising and striking | Something cold and wet
exercise: «A zinger is a sharp, funny line planned to make the other person look silly.» Which words are clues that a zinger is a joke? | *Sharp and funny | Long and tired | Round and blue | Quiet and slow
test: «Ryan's zinger made Mia blush and everyone else giggle.» What does zinger mean? | *A quick, funny remark | A tired yawn | A kind hug | A long walk home
test: Which phrase best fits a witty one-liner that gets a laugh? | Sleep like a log | Walk the dog | Count to ten | *Deliver a zinger
exam: «Her reply was a real zinger, sharp enough to make him laugh and blush.» What is a zinger? | *A sharp, funny, clever remark | A kind, quiet whisper | A long list of rules | A slow, sleepy comment
